      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing works by engaging your vagus nerve through deep, synchronized breaths, which signals your parasympathetic nervous system to shift from a stressed \"fight or flight\" state to a calm \"rest and digest\" mode. This physiological shift naturally reduces cortisol levels and lowers heart rate, effectively dampening your amygdala's internal alarm system. While the specific 4-4-4-4 ratio helps extend the inhalation phase to prevent breathless spikes, the core mechanism is the steady rhythm that trains your autonomic nervous system to prioritize relaxation over reactivity.",
